  "id": "cross-section",
  "term": "cross section",
  "definition": "In fixel-based analysis, cross section is a measure of the size or morphometric extent of a white matter fiber pathway. It is used alongside fiber density and their combined measure to describe tract-specific white matter changes, especially in regions with crossing fibers.",
